This approach efficiently tests for primality by eliminating obvious non-prime candidates first before performing more expensive division operations. The loop runs for sqrt(n)/6 iterations, making it significantly faster than checking all numbers up to sqrt(n).

The implementation correctly handles all test cases including large primes like 999983 which is a known prime number.

